{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Behold, one people.</b> For indeed the negation that frustrates plans and dissuades intentions is the discord that arises among them, whether on account of religions or on account of languages. Now these were one people in the matter of religion, for they were all agreed in the doctrine of the men of the *Tz'Bah* (idolaters), and together with this they were all agreed in language." "<b>And this is what they have begun to do.</b> And likewise this beginning that they have made was now found among them all, with the agreement of all of them." "<b>And now nothing will be withheld from them.</b> If so, nothing prevents them from perfecting their intent, and that idolatry will become universal for the entire human species, and not one of them will turn to know the Creator, blessed be He, and to understand that He is the Former of all. And the reverse of this will come about when there is discord in the matter of the foreign deity, for each one of them will consider that there is an Elohim of elohim to whom all divinities assent, and in Him their order and the order of existence is perfected, as it says: כִּי מִמִּזְרַח שֶׁמֶשׁ וְעַד מְבוֹאוֹ גָּדוֹל שְׁמִי בַּגּוֹיִם (Malachi 1:11)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The abbreviation צא\"בה likely stands for צבא השמים (host of heaven), i.e., astral idolatry; resolved by inference from context."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:29:52.380630244Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}